  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given relation is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8484;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now,</p><p><strong>Reflexive:&nbsp;</strong></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>gcd</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8704;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>Z</mi></math>, hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is not&nbsp;reflexive.</p><p><strong>Symmetric:</strong></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>gcd</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Also,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#8800;</mo><mi>b</mi></math></p><p>Now when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>But,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is not Symmetric</p><p><strong>Transitive:</strong></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p><p>Hence, not transitive</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is neither symmetric nor transitive.</p>"
  }
